      "created_at": "2026-07-30T19:41:31.361Z",
      "text": "-e Machine Learning Unit 1\nSection: Model Evaluation\n\nOverfitting occurs when a machine learning model learns the training data too closely, including noise and details, which leads to poor generalization on unseen validation data.\n\nRegularization techniques such as L1, L2 weight decay, and Dropout are used to prevent overfitting in deep neural networks.",
      "enriched_text": "Document: ml_notes.txt | Section: Notes\nContent:\n-e Machine Learning Unit 1\nSection: Model Evaluation\n\nOverfitting occurs when a machine learning model learns the training data too closely, including noise and details, which leads to poor generalization on unseen validation data.\n\nRegularization techniques such as L1, L2 weight decay, and Dropout are used to prevent overfitting in deep neural networks."
    }
