      "text": "-e Database Management Notes\nSection: Normalization\n\nDatabase normalization is the process of organizing data in a database to reduce redundancy and improve data integrity. Third Normal Form (3NF) requires that every non-key attribute must depend strictly on the primary key.",
      "enriched_text": "Document: db_notes.txt | Section: Notes\nContent:\n-e Database Management Notes\nSection: Normalization\n\nDatabase normalization is the process of organizing data in a database to reduce redundancy and improve data integrity. Third Normal Form (3NF) requires that every non-key attribute must depend strictly on the primary key."
